Right now I'm playing a Tourist (first one I ever tried!) who has had
incredible luck (huge armor store on DL 4 with cloak of displacement,
got GoP and shield of reflection soon after.) I tried a bunch of
weapons, but am currently twoweaponing the +6 Mjollnir and a +1 silver
saber (which I'm going to upgrade as soon as possible.) I'm also going
wishless, which is not a big deal considering I found most of my AK
just lying around. (I've got reflection from SDSM and MR from the
PYEC, so I don't need my shield anymore.) The one thing I think is
going to hurt is that I have only one magic marker, which is rapidly
running out, and I can't wish for any more (as per usual) if I want to
keep my conduct. (I'm also doing genoless and polyless, but I've done
those before.)

Anyway, keep on sacrificing until you get Mjollnir (Frost Brand is
also nice). I highly recommend it. Most nasty monsters are *not*
shock-resistant, and it can cut down a mob of monsters in an
incredibly short time. Also, remember that Tourists can twoweapon. I
normally don't like the whole combat wombat thing, but I feel no guilt
doing it with a Tourist, considering their other disadvantages.

